{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Tablets of stone.</b> Anyone who does not make himself like this stone for engaging in Torah does not merit the words of Torah. Another explanation: stones — because most of the death penalties stated in the Torah are by stoning. Another explanation: in the merit of Jacob, as it is said: ״משם רועה אבן ישראל״. Another explanation: in the merit of the Temple, as it is said: ״הנני יסד בציון אבן״. Rabbi Shimon says: in the merit of King Messiah, as it is said: ״בו חזה הוית עד די אתגזרת אבן די לא בידין״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:38.861369994Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}